---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `This recipe serves four and I am cooking for eleven. Take
the four-person amounts and tell me what I actually need.`;

const Sample = `How many people? 11 [Enter]

For 11 people:
  Flour: 550 g
  Butter: 275 g
  Sugar: 165 g
  Eggs: 5.5`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/unit-1/cc-set-1" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 1
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Recipe Scaler</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> What
            goes in, what gets worked out, what comes out, and{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">every question the brief did not
            answer.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Pick a real recipe with at least three ingredients and put its four-person amounts in your program as variables.</li>
            <li>One number goes in and several come out. <b>Every amount is worked out from the same scale factor</b>, which should be a variable of its own.</li>
            <li>5.5 eggs is a correct answer and a silly one. The brief does not say what to do about it, so you decide, and say so.</li>
            <li>Change the recipe to serve six instead of four. If that is a one-line change you named your variables well.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="success">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={Sample}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">Your recipe will be different. <b>Test 4</b> &mdash; the output should be the original amounts exactly.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program folder, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-recipe-scaler</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
